225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (BETAFLIGHT ALSO PROVIDES TELEMETRY SUPPORT, ALLOWING REAL-TIME TRANSMISSION OF FLIGHT DATA TO THE GROUND STATION OR GOGGLES. THIS DATA CAN INCLUDE BATTERY VOLTAGE, CURRENT CONSUMPTION, GPS COORDINATES, ALTITUDE, AND OTHER VITAL PARAMETERS. BETAFLIGHT ALSO SUPPORTS ON-SCREEN DISPLAY \(OSD\) FEATURES, OVERLAYING FLIGHT INFORMATION DIRECTLY ONTO THE PILOT'S VIDEO FEED FOR ENHANCED SITUATIONAL AWARENESS. WE WERE ABLE TO ADD VOLTAGE/BATTERY WARNINGS AND ALTITUDE AS STATISTICS TO SHOW IN THE BETAFPV DRONE GOGGLE SCREEN.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (BETAFLIGHT ALLOWS FOR THE ACTUAL MAPPING OF THE CONTROLLER JOYSTICK AND BUTTONS TO MOVEMENTS ON THE DRONE. TO DO THIS, THE RECEIVER TAB IS USED ALONG WITH EXPRESSLRS SOFTWARE \(OPENED BY SIGNING INTO THE WIFI EXPRESSLRS WITH PASSKEY EXPRESSION\). HERE, A BINDING PHRASE CONNECTS THE EXPRESSLRS TX MODULE THAT IS INTERNAL OR AN EXTERNAL ATTACHMENT TO THE RADIO, AND A EXPRESSLRS RX RECEIVER FOUND ON THE DRONE. AFTER THIS, THE RECEIVER TAB SHOWS VALUES SUCH AS THROTTLE AND MOVEMENT WHILE TESTING STICK MOVEMENT. FROM THERE, THE MODES TAB ALLOWS TO MAP RADIO CONTROLLER BUTTONS TO FUNCTIONS SUCH AS ARMING THE DRONE \(TURNING ON THE MOTORS\) AND TURNING ANGLE MODE ON OR OFF WHICH RESTRICTS DRONE MOVEMENT.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
