383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (THE FEDERAL AVIATION ADMINISTRATION \(FAA\) HAS SET NATIONWIDE REGULATIONS TO ENSURE THE SAFE OPERATION OF DRONES, INCLUDING THOSE FLYING WITHIN NASHVILLE, TENNESSEE. THESE REGULATIONS APPLY TO BOTH RECREATIONAL AND COMMERCIAL DRONE PILOTS AND ARE INTENDED TO PROTECT PUBLIC SAFETY, PROPERTY, AND AIRSPACE INTEGRITY. ADDITIONALLY, TENNESSEE STATE LAWS AND LOCAL ORDINANCES IMPOSE FURTHER RESTRICTIONS TO ADDRESS PRIVACY CONCERNS, INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY, AND ENVIRONMENTAL PRESERVATION.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (FEDERAL REGULATIONS SET FORTH BY THE FAA APPLY UNIFORMLY ACROSS ALL STATES, INCLUDING TENNESSEE. ANY DRONE WEIGHING MORE THAN 250 GRAMS \(0.55 LBS\) MUST BE REGISTERED WITH THE FAA BEFORE OPERATION, ENSURING ACCOUNTABILITY AND OWNERSHIP TRACKING. RECREATIONAL DRONE PILOTS ARE ALSO REQUIRED TO PASS THE RECREATIONAL UAS SAFETY TEST \(TRUST\), DEMONSTRATING THEIR AWARENESS OF SAFETY PROTOCOLS. DRONE ALTITUDE IS LIMITED TO 400 FEET ABOVE GROUND LEVEL TO PREVENT CONFLICTS WITH MANNED AIRCRAFT, AND OPERATORS MUST MAINTAIN A DIRECT VISUAL LINE OF SIGHT WITH THEIR DRONES AT ALL TIMES. ADDITIONALLY, DRONES CANNOT BE FLOWN DIRECTLY OVER PEOPLE UNLESS THEY MEET SPECIFIC FAA SAFETY CRITERIA. FLIGHTS NEAR AIRPORTS, INCLUDING NASHVILLE INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT \(BNA\), REQUIRE PRIOR AUTHORIZATION THROUGH THE FAA'S LAANC \(LOW ALTITUDE AUTHORIZATION AND NOTIFICATION CAPABILITY\) SYSTEM. DRONES MAY ONLY OPERATE AT NIGHT IF EQUIPPED WITH ANTI-COLLISION LIGHTING VISIBLE FROM AT LEAST THREE STATUTE MILES.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
