388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (WILDLIFE PROTECTION LAWS, AS STATED IN TENNESSEE ADMINISTRATIVE CODE 1660-01-15, PROHIBIT DRONES FROM HARASSING, DISTURBING, OR CAPTURING WILDLIFE. USING DRONES FOR HUNTING, SCOUTING, OR DISTURBING NESTING ANIMALS IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (LOCAL REGULATIONS IN NASHVILLE FURTHER REFINE DRONE USAGE POLICIES TO ADDRESS PUBLIC SAFETY AND ENVIRONMENTAL CONCERNS. THE METRO NASHVILLE PARKS DEPARTMENT PROHIBITS DRONE FLIGHTS IN ALL CITY PARKS EXCEPT FOR DESIGNATED AREAS SUCH AS WARNER PARK, PEELER PARK, AND CANE RIDGE PARK. PILOTS MUST OBTAIN A PERMIT BEFORE FLYING IN THESE DESIGNATED AREAS. SPECIAL EVENT RESTRICTIONS ALSO APPLY, PREVENTING DRONES FROM FLYING OVER OR NEAR LARGE PUBLIC GATHERINGS, SUCH AS CONCERTS, FESTIVALS, OR SPORTING EVENTS, WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL FROM EVENT ORGANIZERS. MANY AREAS MANAGED BY THE U.S. ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS, INCLUDING LAKES AND RESERVOIRS, PROHIBIT DRONE FLIGHTS UNLESS PRIOR AUTHORIZATION IS OBTAINED. RESTRICTED AIRSPACE ZONES INCLUDE GOVERNMENT AND LAW ENFORCEMENT FACILITIES SUCH AS POLICE STATIONS, COURTHOUSES, MILITARY INSTALLATIONS, AND CORRECTIONAL FACILITIES. MAJOR SPORTS AND ENTERTAINMENT VENUES, INCLUDING BRIDGESTONE ARENA AND NISSAN STADIUM, ALSO ENFORCE STRICT NO-FLY ZONES TO ENHANCE SECURITY.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (VIOLATIONS OF DRONE REGULATIONS IN NASHVILLE CAN RESULT IN SIGNIFICANT PENALTIES. THE FAA IMPOSES FINES OF UP TO $27,500 FOR CIVIL VIOLATIONS AND UP TO $250,000 FOR CRIMINAL OFFENSES. AT THE STATE LEVEL, UNAUTHORIZED SURVEILLANCE USING DRONES CAN RESULT IN A CLASS C MISDEMEANOR CHARGE, LEADING TO FINES AND POTENTIAL JAIL TIME. LOCAL ORDINANCE VIOLATIONS, SUCH AS OPERATING A DRONE IN RESTRICTED PARKS OR OVER LARGE GATHERINGS, CAN RESULT IN CITATIONS, FINES, OR EVEN THE CONFISCATION OF THE DRONE.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
